<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/> <meta content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" name="viewport"/><title>Torque Calculator - Force, Lever Arm &amp; Angle | Free Engineering Tool | Free Online Tool</title> <link rel="canonical" href="https://zovo.one/free-tools/torque-calculator/"><meta content="Calculate torque from force, distance, and angle. Convert between N·m, ft·lbs, in·lbs, and kg·cm. Includes bolt torque specs, wrench extension calculator, an." name="description"/><meta content="Michael Lip" name="author"/><meta content="torque calculator, torque formula, newton meters, foot pounds, bolt torque specs, wrench extension, angular acceleration, torque to power, gear ratio, engineering calculator" name="keywords"/><meta content="index, follow" name="robots"/><meta content="2026-03-25" name="date"/><link href="https://zovo.one/favicon.ico" rel="icon"/><meta content="Torque Calculator - Force, Lever Arm &amp; Angle | Free Engineering Tool" property="og:title"/><meta content="Calculate torque with unit conversion, bolt specs lookup, wrench extension calculator, angular acceleration, torque-to-power, and gear ratio multiplication." property="og:description"/><meta content="website" property="og:type"/><meta content="https://tools.zovo.one/torque-calculator/" property="og:url"/><meta content="https://zovo.one/og-image.png" property="og:image"/><meta content="summary_large_image" name="twitter:card"/><meta content="Torque Calculator - Force, Lever Arm &amp; Angle | Free Engineering Tool" name="twitter:title"/><meta content="Calculate torque from force, distance, and angle. Bolt specs, unit conversion, angular acceleration, power, and gear ratios." name="twitter:description"/><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" rel="preconnect"/><link crossorigin="" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" rel="preconnect"/><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700&amp;display=swap" rel="stylesheet"/><script type="application/ld+json"> {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is torque?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Torque is a rotational force that causes an object to rotate about an axis. It equals the force applied multiplied by the perpendicular distance from the axis of rotation (lever arm) and the sine of the angle between them."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the formula for torque?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Torque equals force times distance times sine of the angle: τ = r × F × sin(θ). When the force is perpendicular to the lever arm (θ = 90°), torque is simply τ = r × F."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between torque and power?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Torque is a rotational force measured in N·m or ft·lbs. Power is the rate of doing work and equals torque times angular velocity: P = τ × ω. An engine can produce high torque at low RPM or lower torque at high RPM while delivering the same power."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I convert N·m to ft·lbs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Multiply newton-meters by 0.7376 to get foot-pounds. For example, 100 N·m = 73.76 ft·lbs."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why does a longer wrench make it easier to turn a bolt?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Because torque equals force times distance. A longer wrench increases the lever arm, so less force is needed to produce the same torque."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What torque spec should I use for my bolts?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Torque specs depend on bolt size, grade, and whether they are lubricated. Common values range from about 8 N·m for M6 bolts to over 500 N·m for M24 bolts. Always check the manufacturer specifications for your specific application."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does a gear ratio multiply torque?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A gear ratio multiplies torque proportionally. If the gear ratio is 3:1, the output torque is three times the input torque, but the output speed is one-third of the input speed. This is the fundamental tradeoff in all gear systems."}}]} </script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "WebApplication", "name": "Torque Calculator - Force, Lever Arm & Angle", "description": "Calculate torque from force, distance, and angle. Convert between N\u00b7m, ft\u00b7lbs, in\u00b7lbs, and kg\u00b7cm. Includes bolt torque specs, wrench extension calculator, an.", "url": "https://zovo.one/free-tools/torque-calculator/", "applicationCategory": "EducationalApplication", "operatingSystem": "Web", "offers": {"@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "USD"}, "author": {"@type": "Person", "name": "Michael Lip"}}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://zovo.one/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Free Tools", "item": "https://zovo.one/free-tools/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Torque Calculator - Force, Lever Arm & Angle", "item": "https://zovo.one/free-tools/torque-calculator/"}]}</script><style> *,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0} :root{--bg:#0a0a0f;--surface:#12121a;--border:#1e1e2a;--border-h:#2a2a3a;--text:#e0e0e8;--muted:#8888a0;--accent:#00ff88;--accent-bg:rgba(0,255,136,.1);--link:#00ccff;--radius:12px} body{font-family:'Inter',-apple-system,sans-serif;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);line-height:1.7;min-height:100vh} a{color:var(--link);text-decoration:none}a:hover{text-decoration:underline} .container{max-width:940px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px 20px} h1{font-size:clamp(1.6rem,4vw,2.2rem);font-weight:700;margin-bottom:12px;color:#fff} h2{font-size:1.35rem;font-weight:600;margin:40px 0 16px;color:#fff;padding-bottom:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)} h3{font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:500;margin:20px 0 10px;color:#ddd} p{margin-bottom:14px;color:#ccc} ul,ol{margin-bottom:16px;padding-left:24px;color:#ccc}li{margin-bottom:8px} blockquote{background:var(--surface);border-left:4px solid var(--accent);padding:12px 18px;margin:16px 0;border-radius:6px;font-size:.95rem;color:#b0b0c0} code{background:var(--surface);padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;font-size:.9em} .breadcrumb{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:16px}.breadcrumb a{color:var(--muted)}.breadcrumb a:hover{color:var(--accent)} .badge-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin:16px 0}.badge-row img{height:22px;border-radius:4px} .toc{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:20px 24px;margin:20px 0 30px} .toc h3{margin:0 0 12px;color:var(--accent);font-size:1rem} .toc ul{list-style:none;padding:0;columns:2;column-gap:24px}.toc li{margin:6px 0;break-inside:avoid}.toc a{color:var(--link);font-size:.92rem}.toc a:hover{color:var(--accent)} .visit-widget{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:14px;margin:16px 0;text-align:center}.visit-widget .vcount{font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent)}.visit-widget .vlabel{font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted)} .calc-box{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:28px;margin-bottom:24px} .input-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px;margin-bottom:20px} .input-grid label{display:block;font-size:.82rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px} .input-grid input,.input-grid select{width:100%;background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:11px 14px;color:var(--text);font-family:inherit;font-size:1rem;outline:none} .input-grid input:focus,.input-grid select:focus{border-color:var(--accent);box-shadow:0 0 0 3px var(--accent-bg)} .input-row-3{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:16px;margin-bottom:20px} .input-row-3 label{display:block;font-size:.82rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px} .input-row-3 input,.input-row-3 select{width:100%;background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:11px 14px;color:var(--text);font-family:inherit;font-size:1rem;outline:none} .input-row-3 input:focus,.input-row-3 select:focus{border-color:var(--accent);box-shadow:0 0 0 3px var(--accent-bg)} .btn-calculate{width:100%;padding:14px;background:var(--accent);color:var(--bg);border:none;border-radius:8px;font-family:inherit;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;transition:all .2s} .btn-calculate:hover{background:#33ffaa;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,255,136,.2)} .results-section{display:none;margin-top:24px}.results-section.visible{display:block} .result-hero{background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(0,255,136,.06),rgba(0,204,255,.06));border:1px solid rgba(0,255,136,.2);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:32px 24px;text-align:center;margin-bottom:24px} .result-hero-label{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:4px}.result-hero-value{font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--accent)}.result-hero-detail{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:4px} .result-cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:12px;margin:20px 0} .result-card{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:16px;text-align:center;transition:border-color .2s}.result-card:hover{border-color:var(--border-h)} .result-card-label{font-size:.82rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:4px;font-weight:500}.result-card-value{font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text)}.result-card-unit{font-size:.75rem;color:var(--muted)} .step-box{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:20px 24px;margin:16px 0} .step-title{font-weight:600;color:var(--accent);ma